  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 200 PM MDT SUN AUG 9 2026\nHigh pressure will build over the Desert Southwest as a weak \ntrough moves into the West Coast on Wednesday. This will bring \nsouthwest flow over the region, which will cool temperatures \nslightly, as the high pressure center shifts further east. \nMonsoonal moisture will advect northward, but long range models \nkeep the best chances of associated showers and thunderstorms\nto our south and east through Thursday. By Friday, models \nsubstantially increase precipitation coverage over high terrain \nthrough the weekend. The Central Idaho Mountains and high \nterrain along the Nevada border will see the best chance for \nshowers and thunderstorms (20-40% chance). Warm and breezy \nconditions will continue through the weekend, with temperatures \nslightly below normal through the weekend. High temperatures in \nthe valleys will range from the mid to upper 80s through \nSaturday, with high temperatures in the mountains in the mid to \nupper 70s.",
